README

These examples have been taken from the pico-examples project:

	https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-examples

To build them, you need the pioasm tool in your PATH. You can get and build it
from the Pico SDK with the following commands:

	git clone https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk.git
	cd pico-sdk
	git checkout 2.2.0
	export PICOTOOL_FETCH_FROM_GIT_PATH=/tmp
	mkdir build
	cd build
	cmake ..
	make pioasmBuild
	cp pioasm/pioasm ~/bin	# install it in your personal bin directory

The default LED pin is GPIO4. You may have to update this in the Makefile.
